NetTest is a program which excercises network messaging services. It is
designed for point to point testing between two nodes at a time. One side of
the connection must act as the sender, and the other must act as the receiver.
Specify /r (or -r) on the command line for the receiving side.  Type
NetTest /? for help on the two other options.

By default NetTest will check for the presence of Advanced NetWare and NetBIOS
(or a NetBIOS emulator). If Adv. NetWare is present, it will test message pipe
services, and then IPX and SPX services. If NetBIOS is present, it will then
test datagram and session services. There are command line options available to
force NetTest to perform only either the NetBIOS or the NetWare test (NetTest
/B forces NetBIOS only and NetTest /N forces Advanced NetWare only).

This program was written for testing purposes. It was never meant for public
distribution. If there is suffucient interest, I can make it a more
comprehensive network exerciser and put it on the public domain. Let me know if
you think that would be useful.

